<title>BELGIUM: EU says will request WTO consultations on Indonesia.</title>
<headline>EU says will request WTO consultations on Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had decided to launch a formal complaint with the Geneva-based World Trade Organisation over Indonesia's policy on car imports.</p>
<p>&quot;The EU is concerned at the discrimination against European and other foreign vehicles in favour of national vehicles,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Commission said its decision followed the duty-free importation into Indonesia of a consignment of cars from Korea, believed to have been assembled with Indonesian parts, which took place this week.</p>
<p>&quot;It is something of a paradox that with import tariffs as high as 125 percent, the Indonesian government still feels that it needs discriminatory measures to protect their industry,&quot; Trade Commissioner Sir Leon Brittan said in the statement.</p>
<p>The EU said that the measures adopted by Indonesia breached the basic principles of the multilateral trading system.</p>
</text>
